MojoProof test corpus: notice for the files in tests/corpus/

The files named *.nvptx.ll here are LLVM IR that the Mojo compiler wrote for the GPU kernels of
the Mojo sources listed below (`mojo build --emit llvm --target-accelerator <arch>`). Each file's
row in MANIFEST.tsv records its Mojo version, its flags, its source and the source's sha256. The
IR is compiled from those sources and from the library code they import.

The sources come from the Modular repository, https://github.com/modular/modular, at commit
bbc13a719b6c139ede763f1434a4342ebfd843ac (bbc13a71). Their headers read:

    Copyright (c) 2026, Modular Inc. All rights reserved.

    Licensed under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions:
    https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt

The license text is in LICENSE-APACHE-LLVM, next to this file.

Sources at bbc13a71. Each one's header says "Licensed under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM
Exceptions":

    max/examples/gpu-functions/vector_addition.mojo               vadd/
    max/examples/gpu-functions/reduction.mojo                     reduction/
    max/examples/gpu-block-and-warp/tiled_matmul.mojo             tiled_matmul/
    max/kernels/test/gpu/nn/test_layer_norm.mojo                  layernorm/
    max/kernels/test/gpu/layout/test_layout_mma.mojo              mma/
    max/kernels/test/gpu/linalg/test_multistage_gemm_kernel.mojo  mgemm/, mgemm_nocontract/

The library code that these kernels import comes from the same commit: the Mojo standard library
(Mojo/stdlib/std) and the MAX kernel library (max/kernels/src, max/mojo/max). Every .mojo file
under Mojo/stdlib/std and max/kernels/src carries the same header. So does every .mojo file under
max/mojo/max, except those in the host driver directory max/mojo/max/_driver/max_license/.

Modified copies kept in this repository. Each one keeps Modular's header and says in a comment
what was changed:

    vmul/vector_multiply.mojo      from max/examples/gpu-functions/vector_addition.mojo at
                                   bbc13a71: the kernel renamed and its `+` replaced by `*`
    vsub/vector_subtraction.mojo   from max/examples/gpu-functions/vector_addition.mojo at
                                   bbc13a71: the kernel renamed and its `+` replaced by `-`
    gemv/gemv_f32.mojo             from max/kernels/test/gpu/linalg/test_gemv.mojo at bbc13a71:
                                   reduced to the two float32 launches of its `run_matvec`,
                                   `gemv_kernel` and `gevm_kernel` of max/kernels/src/linalg/gemv.mojo
    gevm_t512/gevm_f32_t512.mojo   from max/kernels/test/gpu/linalg/test_gemv.mojo at bbc13a71:
                                   reduced to one float32 `gevm_kernel` launch, as gemv_f32.mojo
                                   but with 16 warps per block (`tile_size` 512)
    naive_k512/naive_f32.mojo      from max/kernels/test/gpu/linalg/test_multistage_gemm_kernel.mojo
                                   at bbc13a71: reduced to its float32 `matmul_kernel_naive` launch
                                   (BLOCK_DIM 16, transpose_b) at M = 20, N = 256, K = 512
    ../gpu/naive/test_multistage_gemm_kernel.mojo
                                   from max/kernels/test/gpu/linalg/test_multistage_gemm_kernel.mojo
                                   at bbc13a71: a driver of its float32 `matmul_kernel_naive`
                                   launch (BLOCK_DIM 16, transpose_b), its `main` replaced

